> ### Name: drift_data
> ### Title: Construct a longitudinal coordinate-map object
> ### Aliases: drift_data
> 
> ### ** Examples
> 
> d <- data.frame(entity = rep(letters[1:4], 2), time = rep(1:2, each = 4),
+                 x = rep(c(0, 2, 0, 1), 2), y = rep(c(0, 0, 2, 1), 2))
> object <- drift_data(d)
> print(object)
<driftmap> 4 entities; 2 periods; 2 dimensions
Status: unaligned
